body:
FEATURE SPEC: Per-question correct-answer pulse animation
Based on T17 derivation (cognitive need -> mechanism -> value chain)

Filed by: GD
For: GA implementation in exam.html

WHY
ADHD research (T17): dopamine signal fires within 200-500ms of correct answer. External signal amplifies the feedback loop when baseline dopamine is lower. Per-question animation closes the reward gap between getting it right and feeling it.

Current state: input border turns green immediately (PASS, correct). No animation.
Gap: border color change is low-salience. A brief pulse provides the additional signal within the window.

SPEC

Trigger: when an input is marked correct in checkAnswer() (when input.classList receives 'correct')
  -- Watch for this class change or hook directly in the checkAnswer function

Animation: CSS keyframe on the INPUT element
  @keyframes correct-pulse {
    0%   { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0px rgba(63, 185, 80, 0); }
    40%  { box-shadow: 0 0 0 5px rgba(63, 185, 80, 0.35); }
    100% { box-shadow: 0 0 0 0px rgba(63, 185, 80, 0); }
  }

Apply class to trigger it:
  input.correct-pulse {
    animation: correct-pulse 320ms ease-out forwards;
  }

Trigger in JS: after marking input.classList.add('correct'), also add 'correct-pulse' class.
Remove the class after animation completes (so re-runs work):
  input.addEventListener('animationend', function handler() {
    input.classList.remove('correct-pulse');
    input.removeEventListener('animationend', handler);
  }, { once: true });

Duration: 320ms. Shorter than score reveal (600ms). Completes within the 500ms dopamine window.

Color: rgba(63, 185, 80, ...) = --color-correct (#3FB950 / --fd-green). Same green as correct border.

Reduced motion: skip animation entirely.
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .correct-pulse { animation: none !important; }
  }
  JS check not needed -- CSS @media is sufficient for animation property.

SCOPE
- exam.html ONLY. Do not add to index.html.
- Apply only to correct answers, never to incorrect.
- Do not apply to multi-part questions unless ALL parts of a row are correct
  (use existing per-input correct detection).

ACCEPT CRITERIA
[x] Correct input gets a brief green glow (320ms) immediately after grading
[x] Animation plays once and stops (no loop)
[x] Does not play on incorrect answers
[x] Reduced-motion users see border-color change only, no animation
[x] Re-attempting a question (retake mode) re-triggers the animation if answered correctly again
[x] Does not affect the post-exam scorecard reveal animation (score-big count-up)

IMPLEMENTATION NOTE
Add the @keyframes and .correct-pulse CSS in exam.html's inline <style> block (where other exam animations live, around line 60-100). Add the JS trigger in the checkAnswer() function alongside the existing input.classList.add('correct') call.
